Z||000000||86SEFIERO||10-16-2000||01:40 AM||||<BR>Im lookng to replace the piece behind the rear window and above rear fenders and get rid of side windows of the GT and change it into the notchback look While keeping the rear decklid lights nd rear facia f the GT (just like archies purple pavement eater). Can I just swap the two peices or will I have to make modifications? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||10-16-2000||04:25 AM||||I'm guessing you'd have to do some custom work.  Look at the backs of the two and you'll see what I mean.  I think you'd have to change wiring harnesses, too.  Fastback taillights, grilles, etc are much more expensive than notchback hardware.  I guess if you have the time, money and skill go for it (and show us some pics).||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||10-16-2000||08:20 AM||||I've seen pictures of that type of thing before, but have no idea how it was performed. I would think there would be a sizeable amount of modifying.||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||10-16-2000||08:33 AM||||Here's a thought, if you have a fastback clip and a notchback clip, couldn't you just cut and graft? You'd have to do a lot of fiberglass work to bond it together.<P>Just a thought. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
